 + r\u00b2 x + R\u00b2 r - r^3\n\nSimplify left-hand side:\n\nr x R + r\u00b2 x - r R\u00b2 - r\u00b2 R + R^3 + R\u00b2 r - R r\u00b2 - r^3\n\nCombine like terms:\n\nx r (R + r) + (- r R\u00b2 - r\u00b2 R + R^3 + R\u00b2 r - R r\u00b2 - r^3)\n\nSimplify the constants:\n\n- r R\u00b2 - r\u00b2 R + R^3 + R\u00b2 r - R r\u00b2 - r^3\n\n= (- r R\u00b2 + R^3) + (- r\u00b2 R + R\u00b2 r) + (- R r\u00b2 - r^3 )\n\n= R^3 - r R\u00b2 + 0 - R r\u00b2 - r^3\n\n= R\u00b2(R - r) - r\u00b2(R + r)\n\nRight-hand side:\n\n- R\u00b2 x + r\u00b2 x + R\u00b2 r - r^3\n\n= x(- R\u00b2 + r\u00b2) + R\u00b2 r - r^3\n\nNow, set left-hand side equal to right-hand side:\n\nx r (R + r) + R\u00b2(R - r) - r\u00b2(R + r) = x(- R\u00b2 + r\u00b2) + R\u00b2 r - r^3\n\nBring all terms to left-hand side:\n\nx r (R + r) + R\u00b2(R - r) - r\u00b2(R + r) - x(- R\u00b2 + r\u00b2) - R\u00b2 r + r^3 = 0\n\nFactor x terms:\n\nx [ r(R + r) + R\u00b2 - r\u00b2 ] + R\u00b2(R - r) - r\u00b2(R + r) - R\u00b2 r + r^3 = 0\n\nSimplify x coefficient:\n\nr(R + r) + R\u00b2 - r\u00b2 = rR + r\u00b2 + R\u00b2 - r\u00b2 = rR + R\u00b2\n\nConstant terms:\n\nR\u00b2(R - r) - r\u00b2(R + r) - R\u00b2 r + r^3\n\n= R^3 - R\u00b2 r - R r\u00b2 - r^3 - R\u00b2 r + r^3\n\n= R^3 - 2 R\u00b2 r - R r\u00b2\n\nTherefore, equation:\n\nx (rR + R\u00b2) + R^3 - 2 R\u00b2 r - R r\u00b2 = 0\n\nSolve for x:\n\nx = (2 R\u00b2 r + R r\u00b2 - R^3) / (rR + R\u00b2)\n\nFactor numerator:\n\nR(2 R r + r\u00b2 - R\u00b2) = R( r\u00b2 + 2 R r - R\u00b2 )\n\nDenominator:\n\nR(r + R)\n\nTherefore, x = R(r\u00b2 + 2 R r - R\u00b2) / R(r + R) ) = (r\u00b2 + 2 R r - R\u00b2) / (r + R)\n\nTherefore, x = ( -R\u00b2 + 2 R r + r\u00b2 ) / ( R + r ) = ( -(R\u00b2 - 2 R r - r\u00b2) ) / ( R + r )\n\nBut this seems complicated. Let's plug this back into the equation of AC to find y.\n\nEquation of AC: y = m(x - R) = (r / sqrt(R\u00b2 - r\u00b2))(x - R)\n\nTherefore, y = (r / sqrt(R\u00b2 - r\u00b2))( [ (r\u00b2 + 2 R r - R\u00b2 ) / ( R + r ) ] - R )\n\nS