\)) is equal to the area of the fourth triangle \\( S \\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{S_{\\mathrm{a}} + S_{\\mathrm{b}} + S_{\\mathrm{c}} = S}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "Arkady, Boris, Vera, Galya, Danya, and Egor stood in a circle.\n\n- Danya stood next to Vera, on her right side,\n- Galya stood opposite Egor,\n- Egor stood next to Danya,\n- Arkady and Galya did not want to stand next to each other.\n\nWho is standing next to Boris?", "deepseek_reasoning": "Okay, let me try to figure out this problem step by step. So, there are six people standing in a circle: Arkady, Boris, Vera, Galya, Danya, and Egor. The goal is to determine who is next to Boris. Let's break down the given conditions one by one and see how they fit together.\n\nFirst, the circle arrangement. Since it's a circle, each person has two neighbors\u2014one on their left and one on their right. The key here is to determine the order of these six people around the circle based on the given clues.\n\nLet's list out the clues again to make sure I don't miss any:\n\n1. Danya stood next to Vera, on her right side.\n2. Galya stood opposite Egor.\n3. Egor stood next to Danya.\n4. Arkady and Galya did not want to stand next to each other.\n\nStarting with the first clue: Danya is next to Vera, specifically on her right. So if we imagine Vera facing the center of the circle, Danya would be to her right. That means, in the circle, the order would be Vera, then Danya in the clockwise direction. So Vera \u2192 Danya (clockwise). But we need to remember that in a circle, each position is between two people. So Vera's right neighbor is Danya, and Danya's left neighbor is Vera.\n\nSecond clue: Galya is opposite Egor. In a circle of six people, the person opposite someone is three positions away. For example, if Galya is at position 1, Egor would be at position 4 (since 1+3=4, and positions wrap around). So Galya and Egor are directly across from eac